🚀 AWS DevOps Interview Preparation Series — SRE🚀

Topic: Monitoring, Logging, Alerting & Resilience Tools in DevOps

In the world of SRE/Devops, it’s not just about deploying applications — it’s about ensuring they run smoothly, reliably, and resiliently.

 Here’s a quick overview of the tools every SRE & DevOps Engineer should master 👇

Monitoring & Metrics
Keep an eye on system health and performance.
 🔹 Prometheus – Open-source metrics monitoring and alerting.
 🔹 Grafana – Beautiful dashboards for visualization.
 🔹 CloudWatch – AWS native monitoring and logs.
 🔹 Datadog – Full-stack monitoring for cloud applications.

Logging
Track and analyze logs for troubleshooting and insights.
 🔹 ELK Stack (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana) – Centralized log management.
 🔹 Loki – Lightweight log aggregation from Grafana Labs.
 🔹 Splunk – Enterprise-level log analysis and visualization.

Alerting
Get notified before users notice an issue.
 🔹 Alertmanager – Handles alerts from Prometheus.
 🔹 PagerDuty – Incident response and on-call management.
 🔹 Opsgenie – Alerting and escalation management by Atlassian.

Automation
Automate infrastructure, deployments, and scaling.
 🔹 Terraform – Infrastructure as Code (IaC).
 🔹 Ansible – Configuration management and provisioning.
 🔹 Kubernetes – Container orchestration.
 🔹 CI/CD Pipelines – Continuous Integration and Delivery.

Chaos & Resilience
Test how your system behaves under failure.
 🔹 Chaos Monkey – Randomly shuts down instances to test resilience.
 🔹 LitmusChaos – Kubernetes-native chaos engineering.
 🔹 Gremlin – Safe, controlled chaos experiments.

Incident Management
Track, prioritize, and resolve incidents efficiently.
 🔹 Jira – Issue and incident tracking.
 🔹 ServiceNow – ITSM and incident workflow automation.

✅ These tools together help you build a reliable, observable, and self-healing system — which is the core of modern SRE & DevOps.
